nsformation; the README records what capture evidence is required before calling it a verified KMZ round-trip artifact."}, {"id": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan_py_024", "label": "SURGE-PY-024 Pole Placement Integration into the Optimisation Workflow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/artifacts/Surge MVP Ticket Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Placement runs once, only for the recommended candidate, and pole count is deliberately not a PY-018 scoring objective; a generation error fails the detailed workflow with POLE_PLACEMENT / POLE_NETWORK_GENERATION_FAILED rather than returning a successful result with missing poles."}, {"id": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan_py_025", "label": "SURGE-PY-025 Pole GeoJSON + API Presentation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/artifacts/Surge MVP Ticket Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan_additive_v1_contract", "label": "Additive V1 API Compatibility Contract", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/artifacts/Surge MVP Ticket Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "POST /api/v1/optimise is already consumed by Java, so PY-020 extends the response additively instead of silently replacing it: legacy request_id, status, scenario, feeder_routes_geojson and metrics are retained and populated from the recommended candidate while richer fields are added alongside."}, {"id": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan_two_day_demo_sprint", "label": "Two-Day Demo Productisation Sprint", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/artifacts/Surge MVP Ticket Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The sprint turns the completed engine into credible product proof without expanding engineering scope; the demonstration must be narrowed before it is allowed to display synthetic, placeholder or unsupported results."}, {"id": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan_no_false_success", "label": "No False-Success in the Demo Path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/artifacts/Surge MVP Ticket Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An optimiser, persistence or refresh failure must be visible to the user, and synthetic scenario-comparison or parcel-impact values must not be presented as calculated results; every visible engineering value must have a real source."}, {"id": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan_post_mvp_work", "label": "Explicit Post-MVP Work", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/artifacts/Surge MVP Ticket Plan.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Terrain-derived costs, verified KMZ constraint provenance, automatic electrical repair and cable resizing, detailed BoQ, advanced Pareto search, ML ranking, N-1 analysis and production hardening are deliberately deferred beyond the MVP freeze."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan", "target": "docs_artifacts_mvp_minimum_viable_product_py_014", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/artifacts/Surge MVP Ticket Plan.md", "source_location": "Canonical sequence", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan", "target": "docs_artifacts_mvp_minimum_viable_product_py_015", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/artifacts/Surge MVP Ticket Plan.md", "source_location": "Canonical sequence", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_artifacts_surge_mvp_ticket_plan", "target": "docs_artifacts_mvp_minimum_viab